<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia to import 500,000 tonnes sugar in 1997.</title>
<headline>Indonesia to import 500,000 tonnes sugar in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia will import about 500,000 tonnes of sugar in 1997, head of the state logistics agency BULOG, Beddu Amang, said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>&quot;Import volume will depend on the calculation of demand and the development of production. I think we will import around 500,000 tonnes of sugar in 1997,&quot; he told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said Indonesia will produce about 2.5 million tonnes of sugar in 1997, while demand was seen at some 3.0 million tonnes. He gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom + 6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
